    "body": "To test this, one could create several `MessageChannel`s and, without shipping the ports anywhere, post lots of messages without delay, and check that they are evaluated in the same order as they were posted.\r\n\r\nThen do the same but first ship the ports somewhere (and maybe back again). Now relative order between `MessagePort`s should be undefined (since each `MessagePort` has its own task source, the port message queue, and order between task sources is undefined). But an implementation would still be conforming if it kept relative order the same.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
