    "body": "So [this comment](https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=15063#c10) clarifies the intention of the `has_been_shipped` flag, but this part still confuses me:\r\n\r\n> But if you ever send a port through another port, then both the sent port and its paired port, as well as the new port on the other end when the port comes out, have the flag set, and then they start using their own task source just for themselves.\r\n\r\nWhat does \"start using their own task source just for themselves\" mean?",
